Subject: [PATCH 11321/11362] Answer the adversarial review: per-entry marker
 sweep, shape-keyed capstone recovery

The review found two HIGH defects in the work committed as fb56cb8656.

HIGH 1, mutation method. My table deleted three null spellings as ONE
mutation and mutated `beats_majority_vote` nowhere. A grouped deletion
goes RED if any one member is covered, so it says nothing about the
others. A per-entry sweep found 8 of the 13 added marker entries
decorative. Two were redundant by construction and are removed
(`success_verifier_moat` in the relevance tuple, where `verifier_moat`
always matches inside it; `does_not_beat_vote` in the null tuple, where
`not_beat_vote` matches inside it). The other six now have an isolating
test each, one parametrised per null spelling. The sweep reads 12 of 12
RED against this commit.

HIGH 2, the capstone lint exemption. Keyed on the literal "git", it
exempted a rotter that merely mentions the word and refused a recoverer
that reads an archive on disk. Recovery is now recognised by shape: a
`return` between the milestone guard and the sibling `raise` is a
fallback that can still succeed. The only name-keyed exemption left is
the replay helper, which pins its input before the guard. Both
counterexamples are fixtures. A `Return` requirement on the guard `if`
was then found decorative by mutation and removed; the MILESTONE mention
is what spares an ordinary schema guard, and that has a fixture in both
shapes. C1 to C8 all RED with byte-identical restores.

MEDIUM 3, section 3.5 of the note. "19 artifacts" did not reproduce, and
its two exemplars were a tie (exp4221) and a blocked prompt (exp4272).
Re-derived under a stated 31-marker set: 26, all summaries, paths and
names. Recommendation 8.4 (add `experiment` and `title` as claim keys)
is withdrawn: it would flag ties.

MEDIUM 4: the gap statement now names the 3103 artifacts with no
`inference_substrate` at all, the largest silent population.

MEDIUM 5: the wrong "46" reached the `check_substrate_class` docstring in
fb56cb8656, not only the note; corrected in 01fee333ab, recorded in the
note's section 9.

LOW 6: fb56cb8656's message says "none stamped"; read it as "none
stamped BY THIS CHANGE", since exp5008 carries a historical stamp.

LOW 7: SCENARIO-SUBSTRATE-CLASS-1 "SHALL NOT stamp" now has a test that
runs the backfill with apply=True on a warn-only artifact and asserts
the bytes are unchanged.

Step 6 of the error lifecycle: the check that would have caught HIGH 1
is the per-entry sweep itself (scratch script, one deletion per tuple
entry, no groups). It is a method, recorded in the note, not a hook.
Verified: 209 tests pass across the touched files; ruff clean; spec
coverage OK; capstone lint OK on 142 modules.

